WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:10.570
Titania is the largest moon of Uranus and the eighth-largest moon in the Solar System, with a diameter of 1,576 km.

00:11.102 --> 00:19.316
Discovered by William Herschel in 1787, it is named after the queen of the fairies in Shakespeare's A Midsummer Night's Dream.

00:19.951 --> 00:23.133
Its orbit lies inside Uranus's magnetosphere.
